--- body ---
## Context

IDH raid agents run as subprocesses on the host filesystem. A rogue or
confused agent can dirty the main repo, contaminate branches, spiral into
unscoped work, or leak host secrets — all documented incidents in the
harness feedback memory.

Current mitigations are prompt-level (instructions to agents) and
post-hoc (git status checks, discard rogue changes). These work but are
fragile: a sufficiently confused agent ignores instructions.

Firecracker microVMs provide hardware-enforced isolation: each agent gets
its own kernel, tmpfs scratch, and constrained network. The repo is
bind-mounted read-only; only git pushes produce durable state. padme has
KVM (`/dev/kvm` confirmed, AMD SVM). Firecracker cold-starts in 125–150ms
— negligible relative to raid agent runtime.

The isolation is agent-agnostic: any CLI (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, future
agents) runs unchanged inside the VM.

## Motivation (documented incidents)

- Verify agents checkout PR branches in main repo, leaving staged noise
- Parallel execute agents contaminate shared branches
- Verify agents spiral into unscoped harness work after completing verdict

## Design

Each raid agent invocation goes through `scripts/agent-sandbox`:
```
agent-sandbox <agent-cli> [args...]
```
Internally:
1. Firecracker spawns a minimal VM (kernel + rootfs with agent CLI installed)
2. Repo bind-mounted read-only at /repo
3. Writable tmpfs at /workspace (agent's worktree)
4. Outbound network allowed (API calls); inbound blocked via tap interface
5. VM exits when agent process exits — tmpfs evaporates, no trace

## Threat model

| Threat | Current mitigation | With Firecracker | Priority |
|--------|--------------------|-----------------|----------|
| Agent dirties main repo (checked-out files, staged changes) | Post-hoc `git checkout -- .` | Impossible — repo is read-only bind-mount | Medium — annoying, not destructive |
| Agent contaminates shared branch (pushes to wrong branch) | Verify PR file list before merge | Unchanged — git push still works from VM | Low — gate catches this |
| Agent spirals into unscoped work (loops, spawns sub-agents) | Circuit breakers (timeout kill) | Contained to VM; host process tree unaffected | Low — circuit breakers sufficient |
| Agent reads host secrets (API keys, SSH keys, env vars) | None — agent inherits host env | VM gets only explicitly injected env vars | **High** — real risk as projects grow |
| Agent exfiltrates data via network | None | Unchanged — outbound allowed for API | Low — agent already has API access |
| Agent corrupts git history (force-push, rebase main) | Branch protection, verify gate | Unchanged — git remote enforces protection | Low — GitHub enforces this |
| Kernel CVE lets agent escape VM | N/A | Still possible but requires hypervisor exploit | Very low — acceptable residual risk |

**Trigger condition for implementation:** when IDH agents run against projects
containing secrets (SSH keys, API tokens, private research data) that are not
already scoped to the agent's task. Current IDH workload (harness
self-improvement on public repos) does not meet this bar.

## Actions

1. Install Firecracker binary on padme (`scripts/install-firecracker.sh`)
2. Build minimal rootfs image: Debian slim + git + Claude Code CLI + erg binary
3. Write `scripts/agent-sandbox` wrapper (agent-agnostic: takes any CLI)
4. Test: run one raid agent through agent-sandbox, confirm it pushes a branch
5. Wire into beat.py / raid skill: replace direct agent invocation with agent-sandbox
6. Document in STATE.md and CLAUDE.md

## Test

```bash
scripts/agent-sandbox claude --version   # Confirm CLI runs in VM
scripts/agent-sandbox claude -p "echo hi"  # Confirm API reachable from VM
# Then: run a real raid ticket through the sandbox and confirm branch is pushed
```

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `scripts/agent-sandbox` wraps any CLI invocation in a Firecracker VM
- [ ] Repo visible read-only inside VM; tmpfs scratch for writes
- [ ] One raid agent successfully pushes a branch from inside the VM
- [ ] VM leaves no filesystem trace after exit
- [ ] beat.py / raid skill uses agent-sandbox for all agent invocations
